# cahunLicence: Outdoors Card, licences, accreditation, residency and the Hunter Apprenticeship
# Safety Program. Sources: FWCA ss. 1, 63, 64, 66 to 70; O. Reg. 665/98 ss. 1.1, 2 to 13, 18,
# 22 to 24, 25.1, 25.2, 28; Hunting Regulations Summary 2026 (licence, HASP pages). See sources.md.
# Stems ask for a fact a trained candidate knows; every option is a lawful-sounding candidate.
SEG = "LIC"
CAT = "cahunLicence"
Q = [
('Under O. Reg. 665/98, which document must a person already hold before any hunting licence can be issued to them?',
 'An Outdoors Card', ['A licence summary', 'A validation certificate', 'A possession and acquisition licence'],
 'Section 2 says a licence to hunt is not issued to anyone who does not hold an Outdoors Card. The licence summary is what lists the licences once they are issued.'),
('Which of these documents ends on the following December 31 unless another date is shown on it?',
 'A licence to hunt', ['An Outdoors Card', 'Hunter education course proof', 'A landowner consent form'],
 'Under section 17 a licence to hunt runs from the day it is issued to the following December 31 or another day shown on it. An Outdoors Card expires on the date printed on the card.'),
('From what age may the Minister issue an Outdoors Card to a non-resident?',
 '16', ['12', '15', '18'],
 "Anyone at least 16, resident or not, may be issued an Outdoors Card. The exception for ages 12 to 15 applies only to residents, with accreditation and a parent's consent."),
('Which of these is NOT a requirement for a 14-year-old resident to be issued an Outdoors Card?',
 "A licensed mentor's signature", ['Being an Ontario resident', 'Hunter education course proof', 'Consent of a parent they live with'],
 'Section 4 (2) asks for residency, accreditation (such as the course) and the consent of a parent or guardian the young person lives with. A mentor is needed only to hunt as an apprentice.'),
('A member of the Canadian Forces is posted to Ontario. After living here how long are they deemed a resident for hunting?',
 'One month', ['Three months', 'Six months', 'Twelve months'],
 'Section 1.1 deems Canadian Forces and RCMP members stationed and living in Ontario for at least one month to be residents. Others need six of the last 12 months.'),
('Which document counts as proof of accreditation for an Ontario resident buying a licence?',
 'An Ontario hunting licence from 1975', ['A Canadian Firearms Safety Course report', 'An Ontario sport fishing licence', 'A possession and acquisition licence'],
 'Section 12 accepts any Ontario hunting licence issued after January 1, 1968, a pre-2019 hunting Outdoors Card or a ministry verification letter. Firearms documents are not hunting accreditation.'),
('A court order suspends a hunter\'s licence. If the ministry asks, when must they hand back their Outdoors Card?',
 'Immediately', ['Within 10 days', 'Within 30 days', 'When the card expires'],
 'Section 8 says a holder whose licence is cancelled or suspended by a court order must immediately return the Outdoors Card if the ministry requests it. The 10-day rule is for reporting a change of address.'),
('With only the hunter education course and the right licence, which of these may a person hunt with?',
 'A crossbow', ['A rim-fire rifle', 'A 20-gauge shotgun', 'A muzzle-loading rifle'],
 "Section 25.2 applies only to hunting with a gun. Bows and crossbows are not guns, so the course and a licence are enough; any gun also needs a PAL, a minor's licence or CFSC proof."),
('To hunt with a gun, which of these documents is NOT enough on its own?',
 'A hunter education certificate', ['A possession and acquisition licence', "A minor's firearms licence", 'Proof of passing the CFSC and its tests'],
 "Section 25.2 requires a PAL, a minor's licence or proof of passing the Canadian Firearms Safety Course and its tests, carried while hunting with a gun. Hunter education alone covers bows only."),
('How many days does an Outdoors Card holder have to report a new address to the ministry?',
 '10 days', ['7 days', '30 days', '60 days'],
 'Section 6 requires notice of a change in name, address, contact information or residency no later than 10 days after the change.'),
('Which of these is an offence under section 68 of the Act?',
 'Letting a friend use your licence', ['Holding two cards with the same number', 'Carrying a licence issued at age 15', 'Using an Outdoors Card as a small game licence'],
 'Section 68 bans transferring a licence and doing anything to let someone else use it. Two Outdoors Cards with one number are allowed, residents may be licensed at 15, and a card can show the small game licence.'),
('Under section 70 of the Act, what is the status of a licence obtained through a false or misleading statement?',
 'Void', ['Suspended', 'Valid until a court rules', 'Valid for small game only'],
 'Section 70 says such a licence is void, and no one may possess, use or display a void licence. The rule applies to the Outdoors Card too.'),
('Unless the regulations allow more, how many licences to hunt any one species of big game may a person hold?',
 'One', ['Two', 'One per WMU', 'One per open season'],
 'Section 63 of the Act says a person shall not hold more than one licence to hunt any one species of big game, except where the regulations provide otherwise.'),
('What is the youngest age at which a resident may hunt as an apprentice?',
 '12', ['10', '14', '15'],
 'Section 22 lets a resident from age 12 hunt without a licence as an apprentice, holding an Outdoors Card with hunting accreditation and supervised by a licensed adult.'),
('What is the minimum age of the licensed hunter who supervises an apprentice?',
 '18', ['16', '19', '21'],
 'The apprentice must hunt under the direct and immediate supervision of a licensed hunter at least 18 years old who holds a licence for the species.'),
('How many firearms may an apprentice and their supervising hunter carry between them?',
 'One', ['Two', 'Three', 'Two, if one is a bow'],
 'The apprentice may use only the single firearm shared with the supervising hunter, and section 24 (2) bars the supervisor from carrying any other. A bow counts as a firearm under the Act.'),
('An apprentice with no licence of their own shoots a grouse. Whose bag limit does it count against?',
 "The supervising hunter's", ["The apprentice's own", 'Neither, it is extra', "The party's shared limit"],
 'Section 22 (3) says wildlife killed by an apprentice is included in the bag limit of the licensed hunter supervising them.'),
('Which species may an apprentice hunt while supervised?',
 'Those the mentor is licensed for', ['Any small game that is in season', 'Species listed on their own card', 'Any species but big game'],
 'An apprentice may hunt only the species for which the supervising hunter holds a licence to hunt.'),
('A resident aged 13 applies for their own licence. Which of these can the Minister NOT issue to them?',
 'A licence to hunt moose', ['A small game licence', 'A licence to hunt bear', 'A spring wild turkey tag'],
 'Section 23 bars issuing a young apprentice a moose or elk licence, an antlerless deer tag other than an additional tag, or a controlled deer hunt validation. Bear, small game and turkey are not on that list.'),
("Which of these is a condition of the supervising hunter's own licence?",
 'Ensure the apprentice obeys the law', ["Submit the apprentice's report", "Carry the apprentice's card", 'Stay within 5 km of the apprentice'],
 "Section 24 (1) makes it a condition of the supervisor's licence to take all reasonable care that the apprentice complies with the Act and regulations. The 5 km rule is for hunting parties."),
('Which of these may a hunter NOT have on their person while hunting?',
 "A party partner's tag", ['Their own invalidated tag', 'Their printed licence summary', "Their minor's firearms licence"],
 "Section 25.1 bans possessing an Outdoors Card, tag or validation certificate issued to someone else while hunting. Party members hunt on a partner's tag without carrying it."),
('When can an Outdoors Card itself serve as the small game licence?',
 'When both are applied for together', ['When the holder is under 16', 'When hunting on Crown land', 'When the holder is a non-resident'],
 'Section 28 (2) lets the Minister show the small game licence on the Outdoors Card when a person applies for both at the same time. The card then is the small game licence.'),
('North and west of Muskoka and Nipissing, during which dates is a small game licence not valid, except for falconry?',
 'June 16 to August 31', ['April 1 to May 31', 'May 1 to June 15', 'December 1 to March 31'],
 'Section 18 says a small game licence is not valid from June 16 to August 31 in that part of Ontario unless the holder is hunting with a falconry bird.'),
('An Outdoors Card holder moves away and stops being a resident. What does section 6 (2) say?',
 'No resident licences with it', ['The card becomes void', 'Return the card in 10 days', 'Keep resident status to expiry'],
 'A holder who ceases to be a resident must not use the card to get a licence they are no longer eligible for. They must still report the change within 10 days.'),
]
